# promise: #310
# GitHub #310: Cra draws Arc's translate UI from Chromium's translate state, instead of Chrome's
# bubble that showed once when a foreign page first opened. A Russian page is offered (no bubble);
# the sidebar's URL field says "Translation Available" for as long as the page can be translated;
# it opens Arc's popover (Options, Translate), whose Translate starts a translation that ends
# translated (online) or with Arc's error toast (offline). Chromium offers translation only with
# a Google API key (release builds have one, CRA_GOOGLE_API_KEY), so the run sets a stand-in.
env GOOGLE_API_KEY=cra-scenario
cra://open?url=${PAGE}/../translate.html
expect-log loaded 127.0.0.1
expect-log translate: offer ru→en
wait 1
cra://debug?translate=line
expect-log translate line: Translation Available
cra://debug?cdp=Cra.getTranslateState&params={}
expect-log Cra cdp Cra.getTranslateState .*"available":true
cra://debug?translate=open
expect-log translate popover: Translate this page to English\? \| Options, Translate
cra://debug?translate=menu
expect-log translate menu: Choose Another Language, Never Translate This Site, \|, Language Settings
cra://debug?translate=press:Translate
expect-log translate: (translated|error) ru→
# An English page has no line.
cra://open?url=${PAGE}
wait 3
cra://debug?translate=line
expect-log translate line: none
